        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 84-year-old male admitted on 01/05/2020 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and blood tests confirmed the exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, with close monitoring of vital signs and pulse oximetry. He responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. He is discharged on an optimised inhaler regimen and a short course of oral prednisolone. I recommend close follow-up in your practice and review of his long-term COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
